{"diagnosis": "Loopback TX stayed idle so RX sampled 0xff instead of 0xa5 (TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xff want 0xa5, sha 2e5ce049369d). Reset loads send_pattern<=~1 with send_dummy<=1 and reg_div_we re-arms dummy, then the send_dummy && !send_bitcnt branch loads 15 idle bits with send_pattern<=~0 and blocks reg_dat_we because send_bitcnt!=0 per excerpt. With divider 64 this dummy window swallows the 0xa5 write from picosoc/picosoc.v:201 reg_dat_we, leaving ser_tx=send_pattern[0]=1 idle per picosoc/simpleuart.v:20 cone.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -113,15 +113,10 @@
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			send_pattern <= ~1;
+			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
-			send_dummy <= 1;
 		end else begin
-			if (send_dummy && !send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= ~0;
-				send_bitcnt <= 15;
-				send_divcnt <= 0;
-				send_dummy <= 0;
-			end else
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
", "expected": "tohost PASS with uart loopback 0xa5 received correctly (no TRAP: uart data mismatch)"}

